{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs3621TmeJWvLZFxoTAn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is in. `get_metadata_for_wheel()` now reads the wheel's own `{name}-{version}.dist-info/METADATA` instead of the first `.dist-info/METADATA` in the archive. A vendored dist-info that sorts first no longer wins. Nothing is committed.\n\n**What changed**\n\n- **`src/fromager/pkgmetadata/pep376.py`** (new): `verbatim_dist_name()` and `dist_info_name()`. Both validate with `parse_wheel_filename` first, so bad names and non-`.whl` extensions raise `InvalidWheelFilename`. The version is taken from the filename string, not from `Version`, so it stays verbatim. Both are exported from `fromager.pkgmetadata`.\n- **`src/fromager/candidate.py`**: new `_wheel_metadata_path(url)`. The fallback reads exactly that member and raises `ValueError` if it's missing.\n- **`src/fromager/wheels.py`**: `extract_info_from_wheel_file` uses `verbatim_dist_name` instead of `split(\"-\", 1)[0]`.\n- **`src/fromager/dependencies.py`**: `_get_metadata_from_wheel` uses `dist_info_name`, which drops its own split and the now-unused `parse_wheel_filename` import.\n- **Tests**: `tests/test_pep376.py` (new) covers the helpers, verbatim casing and versions, build tags, and rejected filenames. `tests/test_pep658_support.py` gains tests for the URL path logic and the fallback. One builds a zip where a vendored dist-info comes first and asserts the wheel's own METADATA is returned. Another asserts `ValueError` when only a vendored dist-info exists.\n\n**Decisions to review**\n\n- `_wheel_metadata_path` percent-decodes the filename. PyPI encodes `+` in local versions as `%2B`, so without decoding those wheels would never match their zip member.\n- `dependencies.py` uses `dist_info_name` rather than only `verbatim_dist_name`. It replaces both the name split and the version logic, so the two call sites now share one path.\n- A non-wheel URL passed to the fallback now raises `InvalidWheelFilename` rather than `ValueError`, since the filename is validated before the zip is read.\n\n**Verification**\n\n- `pytest` over `test_pep376`, `test_pep658_support`, `test_dependencies`, `test_wheels`, `test_pkgmetadata`, `test_bootstrapper`, `test_resolver`, and `test_sbom`: 156 passed, 2 skipped.\n- `ruff format` and `ruff check` are clean on the changed files.\n- `mypy -p fromager` reports 2 errors, both in `resolver.py` lines 1186 and 1309 that I didn't touch. They predate this change.\n- I didn't run the full test suite, because CLAUDE.md says to ask first."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4946,"cache_read_input_tokens":112982,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4946},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"13ec0ed9-053c-412d-a45d-9f05a42f56e3","uuid":"00512a57-9532-4415-b13b-e1c31e197dc4","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:12:35.128Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs361ibVoVMbE4q5CZ3x"}
